SM-T715 tablet (arm64 image): quick settings without the phone's tiles.

Drops mobile data, torch, location, NFC and fingerprint from the tile
catalogue (no modem driver on arm64 yet; GNSS, the flash LED and NFC are
not driven; no fingerprint sensor), so they show neither in the sheet nor
under "Add tiles"; a saved layout that names them loses them (sanitize()
skips unknown ids). Hotspot stays under "Add tiles", and Rotation
(upstream's rotation lock, over omamobile-autorotate.service, which the
image's t715-rotate serves) is back in the default layout. test/
tiles-model.js follows. From the owner's Lenovomarchy port's
0001-tablet-quick-settings-tiles (which drops hotspot and the rotation lock
too) and the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series (0001, 0005, 0007). Against
omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), packages/omamobile-shell
(applied with patch -p1 in that directory).

